==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{m|frm|inextricable}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|inextricabilis}}.

===Adjective===
{{head|en|adjective}}

# {{lb|en|of a knot etc}} Impossible to [[untie]] or [[disentangle]].
#*{{quote-journal
|en
|year=2020
|author=Joel Swanson
|title=Are anti-Semitism fears stopping Jewish Dems from supporting Bernie Sanders?
|journal=The Forward
|passage=And when it comes to far-right anti-Semitism, hatred of Jews is '''inextricable''' from opposition to socialism.}}
# {{lb|en|of a problem}} Impossible to [[solve]].
# {{lb|en|of a maze etc}} Impossible to [[escape]] from.

